    <td style="vertical-align: top; text-align: left"><p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">The number of DSUs and PSUs granted to each NEO was determined based on a certain percentage of their annual base salary, consisting of 100% for our CEO and 50% for our other two NEOs. </p>
                                                      <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">&#160;</p>
                                                      <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">While the mix of our LTI program consisted of 50% DSUs and 50% PSUs, the vesting of the PSUs was revised from achievement of relative total stockholder return performance goals to Xtant stock price goals over a three-year performance period.</p>
                                                      <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">&#160;</p>
                                                      <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">We used a 30-day volume weighted average price of our common stock to determine the number of DSUs and PSUs to grant. Accordingly, the grant date fair value of these awards may be different than the value we used in determining the number of RSUs or DSUs. </p>
                                                      <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">&#160;</p>
